First of all my definition of shallow is the mines, sokoban (no bones), 
and DoD up until the quest entrance. To have quest artifact on these 
levels would mean:

Post quest character has entered the mines. Why and how often?
Ascending character has died in DoD between level 4 and quest entrance. 
How often?

Secondly I doubt that many charcters die in DoD post quest pre Medusa. 
So I could extend my shallow to include the Medusa level.

And so what! My opinion is that bones system is for greate rewards, 
tough opponents or big disapointments[1].


My thoughts on fountain wishes:

IMHO most fountain wishers are scummers. They don't respect their 
characters at all but disregarding all dangers are trying to get a 
fountain wish. Are we to condone this type of play?

If we restrict quest artifact wishes, there still are other artifacts 
and non-artifact items such as S or GSDM to wish.


On wishing of quest artifacts:

IMHO too great rewards for fountain scumming but for those that really 
want to have them: prepare thyself!

Why a restriction on wishing ones own quest artifact: One still has to 
get the Bell. In this case I wouldn't bring the owner with the artifact 
but the quest nemesis[2].


[1] I've seen a totaly empty level with a ghost that had only long 
sword[3], some armor and some tools junk (no bags at all) that I already 
had. He'd choked on his food.

[2] On the other hand one could take the fight on ones own ground but on 
the other the nemesis would carry the artifact and thus benefit from it. 
IMHO these balance each other out.

[3] This probably had been the Excalibur but as my character owned one 
